# hui AIR 214+MK "PLASMA TRAP" — the CONTACT explosion (14z-82d).
# 87's twin with the spacing INVERTED: 87 walks both fighters apart so the
# mine detonates by TIMER (its header explains why contact is "a different
# code path" — this rig IS that other code path, on purpose).
#
# WHY (maintainer playtest report, hui30 — RESOLVED 14z-82d, see STATE):
# air 214+MK "has sfx now". MEASURED OUTCOME: the sfx is NOT a hui30
# delta — ring A/B on 87 AND on this rig is byte-identical hui29 vs
# hui30, and hui29's timer rig demonstrably fires the trap (type-69 pool
# spawns f3432/f4232) and sounds its detonation (id 0x049A at
# f3571/f3716). The "new" MK sfx is the 14z-79 (b') fix's restoration:
# pre-hui29 the MK detonation CRASHED the machine before its sound (the
# reproducing input was MK specifically), which is exactly why the sound
# is new to the ear and MK-only. ALSO MEASURED HERE: the trap = pool
# type 69, and the hit-class sweep is POOL-vs-POOL (both loop registers
# stride pool slots; the f7997 crash regs sit in the pool on both
# sides) — a trap hitting a FIGHTER never transits the extended map, so
# the hitclass fix cannot change trap-vs-fighter audio.
#
# STATUS: the CONTACT event (mine overlapping another POOL object) is
# still unproduced by this rig (0 map entries on both cuts — the v1 P2
# walk-through and the v2 stationary-P2 shapes). Kept as the starting
# point for a pool-vs-pool contact rig (needs an opposing PROJECTILE to
# clash with, e.g. P2 Victor doing a pool-object move into the mine —
# not a walking fighter). DO NOT promote to a gate until the map probe
# fires ≥1 (87's rule: a green that produced no event proves nothing).
#
# THE SPACING (the 83c/87 lesson, applied in reverse): fighters stay
# NEAR CENTER — no corner walks — and P2 nudges TOWARD the landing spot
# after the throw, so the mine lands/rolls INTO P2 and explodes on
# contact. MK only (the maintainer's observed strength; 87 covers the
# strength sweep for the timer path). Two spaced attempts, insurance
# against a seq-thunk-eaten frame-pinned input (87's rule).
#
# BOTH SIDES POKED: P1 = Huitzil (0x10), P2 = Victor (0x03 on vsav AND
# vsav2). Early window only (replay-80 rule).
